<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wannsee Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wannsee Conference was a meeting of senior Nazi officials held at a villa on the Wannsee lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on 20 January 1942. Chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a>, it coordinated the government ministries and SS offices involved in the 'Final Solution', the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> and murder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The surviving minutes, kept by Adolf Eichmann, are a key document of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference.jpg" alt="Wannsee Conference" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A.Savin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haus_der_Wannsee-Konferenz_02-2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In occupied Europe, mobile killing units of the Einsatzgruppen shot Jews in the Soviet territories from 1941, and the <b>Wannsee Conference</b> of January 1942 coordinated the deportation of Jews from across the continent to extermination camps in occupied Poland: Chełmno, Bełżec, Sobibór, Treblinka, Majdanek and Auschwitz-Birkenau.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
